degree(DifferentialModule) -- returns the degree of the differential
********************************************************************

  * Function: *note degree: (Macaulay2Doc)degree,
  * Usage: 
        degree D
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note differential module: DifferentialModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

This method returns the degree of the differential of a differential module. In
more detail: since the source and target of the differential are required to be
equal, we must specify the degree of the differential in order for the
differential to be homogeneous; this method returns that degree.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x]/(x^3)                    |
|                                        |
|o1 = R                                  |
|                                        |
|o1 : QuotientRing                       |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : phi = map(R^1, R^1, x^2, Degree=>2)|
|                                        |
|o2 = | x2 |                             |
|                                        |
|             1      1                   |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                    |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = differentialModule phi         |
|                                        |
|      1      1      1                   |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R                    |
|                                        |
|     -1     0      1                    |
|                                        |
|o3 : DifferentialModule                 |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : degree D == {2}                    |
|                                        |
|o4 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note differential(DifferentialModule): differential, -- returns the
    differential of a differential module

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note degree(DifferentialModule): degree_lpDifferentialModule_rp, --
    returns the degree of the differential
