unfold -- converts a differential module into a 1-periodic complex
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        unfold(D,a,b)
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note differential module: DifferentialModule,, 
      * a, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * b, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 

Description
===========

Given a differential module D and integers a and b, this method produces a
chain complex with the module D in homological degrees a through b, where all
maps are the differential of D.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : phi = matrix{{0,1},{0,0}};                                         |
|                                                                        |
|              2       2                                                 |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = differentialModule(phi);                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : unfold(D,-3,4)                                                     |
|                                                                        |
|       2       2       2       2       2       2       2       2       2|
|o3 = ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ |
|                                                                        |
|     -3      -2      -1      0       1       2       3       4       5  |
|                                                                        |
|o3 : Complex                                                            |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note differentialModule(Complex): differentialModule_lpComplex_rp, --
    converts a complex into a differential module
  * *note resMinFlag: resMinFlag, -- gives a minimal free flag resolution of a
    differential module of degree 0
  * *note resDM: resDM, -- uses a "killing cycles"-style construction to find a
    free resolution of a differential module
  * *note foldComplex: foldComplex, -- converts a chain complex into a
    differential module

Ways to use unfold:
===================

  * "unfold(DifferentialModule,ZZ,ZZ)"

